<Window x:Class="VaccineAssist.Desktop.MainWindow"
        xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        Title="Vaccine Assist"
        Width="1000" Height="650"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterScreen">
    <!--
        V-T-single-nav (Will, 2026-09-14, verbatim: "I also asked for all
        the tabs in the app to match exactly what is in the cloud too,
        currently they dont. You have an extra row of tabs that are all
        showing the same screen (that matches the cloud). Remove that
        extra row of tabs."): MainWindow now hosts exactly ONE
        CloudPageView, filling the whole window — the cloud app's OWN top
        nav (see cloud/lib/nav-config.ts / app/top-nav.tsx) is the only
        tab row now. The previous six-TabItem TabControl (Scheduling/Data
        entry/Lots/Active vaccines/Ordering/Physicians — five of which
        each hosted their OWN CloudPageView, duplicating the cloud's nav
        five times over) is gone; data entry stays reachable via
        Ctrl+NumPad7, the tray menu, and the Pioneer overlay icon
        (DataEntryPopupWindow, unchanged) rather than a native tab.

        The previous native "Sign out" bar above the tabs is removed too,
        for the same "no extra row above the cloud's own nav" reason —
        the cloud's account menu (top-nav.tsx) has its own sign-out, and a
        full desktop-level sign-out (clearing the persisted 90-day
        session) is still one click away from the tray menu's own
        "Sign out" item (Tray/TrayMenuBuilder.cs).

        MainContent's Content is set in code-behind to the CloudPageView
        instance App.xaml.cs already built, initialized, and (for a fresh
        sign-in) handed off to the cloud's session — see
        App.xaml.cs's PrepareMainCloudPageViewAsync and this window's own
        constructor — BEFORE this window was even shown.
    -->
    <ContentControl x:Name="MainContent"/>
</Window>
